Third-party software
--------------------
Dependencies are installed by uv and pnpm and keep their own licenses; none are vendored in this repository.
One of them is not under an open-source license:

- Remotion (remotion, @remotion/*), used for the Cinema Studio cut preview, is under the Remotion License:
  free for individuals and companies of up to three people, a paid company license otherwise.
  See https://www.remotion.dev/license.

ComfyUI (GPL-3.0) is not included or linked: the studio talks to a separately installed ComfyUI over its
HTTP API. The workflow files in workflows/comfy/ are API-format graphs written for this project.

Models
------
No model weights are included. Models run through ComfyUI are downloaded separately and keep their own
licenses, for example Wan 2.2 TI2V 5B (Apache-2.0), FLUX.2 klein 4B (Apache-2.0) and LTX-2.5 (LTX-2
Community License). Each model's license is noted in its registry file (registry/models/, license_tier).
Hosted models (fal.ai, Google, Runway, ElevenLabs and others) are used under each provider's terms with your
own API keys.

Media
-----
The test fixtures in fixtures/ are synthetic test patterns made with ffmpeg or media generated with AI models.
The pictures and clips in apps/web/public/ (template covers, character designer, starter, Faceless previews) were
generated with AI models through this studio, and the voice samples in apps/web/public/voices/ with ElevenLabs
Eleven v4 through it. The logo, the screenshots in docs/screenshots/ and the Wan 2.2 5B sample in docs/demo/ are this project's own. The launch film
linked from the README was made with this studio too; its whoosh, click, riser and impact sounds are from Pixabay,
used under the Pixabay Content License.
None of them shows a real person.
